{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false},"description":"Returns deterministic similarity and identity hashes for one local file read once in memory: whole-file sha256 and md5 (node:crypto), tlsh (clean-room TLSH over the whole file; null under 50 bytes or too uniform), and ssdeep (clean-room CTPH/SpamSum). When the bytes are an executable image it adds imphash and imphash_sorted (pefile-exact PE import hash; delay imports excluded; ordinal-only imports resolved via the ws2_32/wsock32/oleaut32 tables else ord<N>), rich_pe_hash (MD5 of the PE Rich-header clear bytes), telfhash (TLSH over ELF .dynsym global STT_FUNC names after dropping leading .,_,str,mem and trailing 64), symhash (MD5 of the sorted Mach-O external-undefined symbol names), and per_section_sha256 over file-backed sections (bounded, with coverage). An optional slice selects one universal-binary architecture; import/symbol/section hashes then cover only that slice. It never executes the target, uses no network, writes no file, recovers no key or plaintext, and evaluates no trust; input is bounded to 256 MiB. Each hash whose inputs are absent is reported as null (never omitted) with a matching limitation, and a shared value is consistent with structural resemblance, not proof of shared provenance.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"examples":[{"path":"/artifacts/application"},{"path":"/artifacts/application","slice":"arm64"}],"properties":{"path":{"description":"Absolute filesystem path to the selected local file","minLength":1,"pattern":"^[^\\x00]*$","type":"string"},"slice":{"description":"Architecture of the Mach-O universal slice to analyze; defaults to the first declared slice","enum":["x86","x86_64","arm","arm64","powerpc"],"type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"},"name":"compute_similarity_hashes","outputSchema":{"$defs":{"__schema0":{"pattern":"^ev_[a-f